# aiter tuned fmoe row: FlyDSL MoE stage-2 kernel for the 16384-token prefill tier
#
# Base:        /sgl-workspace/aiter @ d9e5ef7ce08ee7045d583aed768cff41aa9210fe (clean).
#              This file does not exist at that commit -- the patch is a pure addition, so the
#              base is "absent" and no pristine copy was needed. `git -C /sgl-workspace/aiter
#              status --short` before the change showed only the runtime's own
#              `aiter/jit/flydsl_cache/`.
#
# Apply:       git -C /sgl-workspace/aiter apply /work/patches/rejected/0003-aiter-tuned-fmoe-prefill-16384.patch
#              (equivalently: cp analysis/qwen3_8_2_4t_a95b_mxfp4_tuned_fmoe.csv \
#                                /sgl-workspace/aiter/aiter/configs/model_configs/)
#              MUST be in place BEFORE the server starts: aiter's config lookup is
#              lru_cached per process and the merged /tmp/aiter_configs/tuned_fmoe.csv is
#              rebuilt only at import.
#
# What it does:
#   aiter's `fused_moe` has no tuned row for this model, so at every token tier it logs
#   `no tuned FlyDSL config for (...)` and falls back to a token-count if-ladder in
#   fused_moe.py. This adds the one row for the tier that dominates prefill. With
#   --chunked-prefill-size 16384 and get_padded_M = nextPow2, essentially every extend chunk
#   keys on token=16384; the EXTEND trace confirms it (818 launches of the tile_m=64 kernels
#   for 802.6 ms, against 92 launches / 61.1 ms of tile_m=128). Only stage 2 changes:
#     heuristic: moe1 ..._t64x128x256_w4_bnt0 | moe2 ..._t64x128x256_atomic
#     tuned:     moe1 ..._t64x128x256_w3_bnt0 | moe2 ..._t64x256x256_atomic_persist
#   The stage-1 swap is cosmetic (_w2/_w3/_w4_bnt0 are within 0.15% of each other).
#
# Kernel-level measurement (analysis/tune_flydsl_moe.py, standalone, this model's exact MoE
# shape, interleaved medians per tuning-core/measurement.md Rule 6b):
#   heuristic pair   1130.16 us   spread 4.24%
#   tuned pair       1109.95 us   spread 4.47%      -> 1.0182x
#   Reproduced across four independent races: 1.0211x (80x129 candidate subspace),
#   1.0195x (full 272x257 space), 1.0207x/1.0201x (head-to-head, ksplit=-1),
#   1.0194x/1.0182x (head-to-head, ksplit=0, the value production uses).
#
# Engagement (verified live, not inferred): with the row installed the server log flips from
#   [fused_moe] no tuned FlyDSL config for ('gfx950', 256, 16384, ...)
# to, on all 8 ranks,
#   [fused_moe] using 2stage (kernelName1='flydsl_moe1_afp4_wfp4_bf16_t64x128x256_w3_bnt0',
#               kernelName2='flydsl_moe2_afp4_wfp4_bf16_t64x256x256_atomic_persist')
#               for ('gfx950', 256, 16384, 8192, 2048, 64, 9, ...)
#   (requires AITER_LOG_TUNED_CONFIG=1, which the image already sets; the *miss* line is
#   unconditional, the *hit* line is not.)
#
# End-to-end measurement -- WHY THIS IS IN rejected/:
#   local pooled baseline   1266.119 tok/s  (n=8 across two server instances, spread 1.03%)
#   this arm                1266.767 tok/s  (n=4, one instance, spread 0.59%)   -> +0.05%
#                           1268.263 tok/s  (n=3, dropping the first run against a fresh
#                                            server, spread 0.19%)              -> +0.17%
#   TTFT                    10966.47 ms vs baseline 10967.4 ms                  -> -0.01%
#   TPOT                    39.78 ms mean vs baseline 39.87 ms
#   gsm8k 5-shot strict-match: 0.979530 +/- 0.003900   (gate: baseline 0.978014 +/- 0.004039;
#                                                       delta +0.0015, inside stderr -- PASS)
#
#   The null result was PREDICTED BEFORE the server was restarted, and the prediction is the
#   point: the two tile_m=64 MoE kernels are 13.0% of prefill (802.6 of 6166.6 ms of extend
#   GPU span) and prefill is 21.2% of wall (TTFT 10967 ms of a 51754 ms per-request budget),
#   so 1.9% off those kernels is 0.05% end to end -- nineteen times below the noise floor.
#   Measured: +0.05%. The kernel win is real, live and reproducible; it simply has nowhere
#   near enough leverage to be a throughput win on this workload, and claiming it as one
#   would be claiming noise.
#
# Not stacked with anything. Independent of patches/rejected/0001 (bf16 dense GEMM table),
# which touches a different aiter config file and a different set of kernels.
#
diff --git a/aiter/configs/model_configs/qwen3_8_2_4t_a95b_mxfp4_tuned_fmoe.csv b/aiter/configs/model_configs/qwen3_8_2_4t_a95b_mxfp4_tuned_fmoe.csv
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..13317c70a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/aiter/configs/model_configs/qwen3_8_2_4t_a95b_mxfp4_tuned_fmoe.csv
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+gfx,cu_num,token,model_dim,inter_dim,expert,topk,act_type,dtype,q_dtype_a,q_dtype_w,q_type,use_g1u1,doweight_stage1,block_m,ksplit,us1,kernelName1,err1,us2,kernelName2,err2,us,run_1stage,xbf16,flat,tflops,bw,_tag
+gfx950,256,16384,8192,2048,64,9,ActivationType.Silu,torch.bfloat16,torch.float4_e2m1fn_x2,torch.float4_e2m1fn_x2,QuantType.per_1x32,1,0,64,0,0,flydsl_moe1_afp4_wfp4_bf16_t64x128x256_w3_bnt0,0.0%,0,flydsl_moe2_afp4_wfp4_bf16_t64x256x256_atomic_persist,0.0%,1109.95,0,0,0,0,0,
